ype {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8455dd35-3ef6-5817-8bd5-bd6711371ecf" :question/math-academy-id "q-337400" :question/problem "Suppose we would like to find an integrating factor to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\n2xy\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation using an integrating factor. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(x)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{x}.$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=2xy,\\,Q(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={{field-3}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={{field-4}}\n$$\n\nSince for this equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})={{field-5}},\n$$\n\nwhich depends on $x$ only, then an integrating factor for our equation is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-6}},\n$$\n\nand we arrive at the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-7}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x).\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=2xy,\\,Q(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy)=2x \\\\ \\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}) & =2x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis a function of $x$ only, we conclude that an integrating factor is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡({x}^{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the differential equation by the integrating factor gives\n\n$$\n{e}^{{x}^{2}}(2xy\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363924 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7cbedeed-6ac6-5ed8-bd25-9a85eda9577b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Integrating Factor for an Inexact Equation: Condition on X Satisfied"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e671584-d714-599e-bdbb-83396e8a9863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363926} {:answer/id #uuid "4f42ec69-2bbe-5a19-a5b5-e62d525639c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363927} {:answer/id #uuid "722974b8-cefd-5b58-b66c-626666f0e9e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363928} {:answer/id #uuid "3f335fa9-8436-5fa8-bf15-f22fd8326631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f42ec69-2bbe-5a19-a5b5-e62d525639c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363927} :answer-field/id #uuid "fed192f1-d7ca-5c64-b0e8-23a0458dd608" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363925} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6937c6ba-108f-5951-ab9d-d917a5b886c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363931} {:answer/id #uuid "cc7