nswer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75b8460d-0da5-5d39-bd5d-149dd11a57ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363951} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a02851-5e5d-5eed-b4f8-753c16a6fb79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363952} {:answer/id #uuid "8f1f0fa6-4984-596e-b91c-e38eb30b8b1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363953} {:answer/id #uuid "60695574-9422-5437-8853-fe237cdc196a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f1f0fa6-4984-596e-b91c-e38eb30b8b1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363953} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a69fbdd-8f55-574f-81c8-88ccda39b151" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363950} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2971f26-c02d-5832-afaa-f5a1721ad801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363956} {:answer/id #uuid "c876a464-c4f2-5648-827d-7f291b4aea78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363957} {:answer/id #uuid "e3959a65-1382-5c60-bfb3-5ac7c0c31454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363958} {:answer/id #uuid "233691c1-5f08-5960-8251-1e6d6a17e2ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3959a65-1382-5c60-bfb3-5ac7c0c31454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363958} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fb71082-75a1-51b8-99e3-9d63b152cced" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363955} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a401d42d-3826-5997-8569-74079f9cf660" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-{x}^{2}}((2-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363961} {:answer/id #uuid "a141ea21-787d-5197-bc95-1dc0153e1c5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}}((2-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363962} {:answer/id #uuid "e26a39bb-d6a6-545b-9204-279ab382b789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}((2-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363963} {:answer/id #uuid "9182a703-273c-5e42-a361-5091080e45a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}((2-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e26a39bb-d6a6-545b-9204-279ab382b789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}((2-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363963} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c431362-6a62-5441-927e-177427b5de5e" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c9f9f6ec-3614-51f5-8a8c-4b576b94a5aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-337476" :question/problem "Suppose we would like to find an integrating factor to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3y-2\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation using an integrating factor. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(x)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{x}.$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in differential form. This gives\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=2-3y,\\,Q(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\,{{field-4}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\,{{field-5}}\n$$\n\nSince for this equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})={{field-6}},\n$$\n\nwhich depends on $x$ only, then an integrating factor for our equation is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-7}},\n$$\n\nand we arrive at the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-8}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(x)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{x}.$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in differential form: \n\n$$\n(2-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nLet's denote \n\n$$\nP(x,y)=2-3y,\\,Q(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2-3y)=-3 \\\\ \\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}) & =\\frac{1}{1}(-3-0) \\\\  & =-3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis a function of $x$ only, we can conclude that an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int -3\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-3x) \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand by multiplying our differential equation by the integrating factor, we have\n\n$$\nI(x)\\cdot ((2-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=I(x)\\cdot 0\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n{e}^{-3x}\\cdot ((2-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=0.\n$$"}]}
